Origin: a local fix of the qemu-gui-manager author, not upstream.
qemu-gui-manager ships it, and File > Build QEMU applies it to the
virglrenderer it builds with DRM native context.

amdgpu: force write-combining for host-visible blob mappings

Report write-combining for all mappable host-visible blobs in the AMDGPU
native context. Write-back caching of host blobs causes severe CPU-write
stalls over virtio-gpu native context: radeonsi/RADV upload & staging
buffers (GTT, allocated without AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_CPU_GTT_USWC) are used
by the compositor to texture-upload client backing stores, and streaming
CPU writes into a WB-cached mapping of a host blob stall badly. Visible
symptom: Qt/QWidget apps stutter, lag grows with window size.

In practice this only changes GTT buffers that were previously CACHED;
VRAM and USWC-tagged buffers already mapped WC.

Requires QEMU '-accel kvm,honor-guest-pat=on' so the guest's WC PAT is
honored by KVM. Trade-off: slower CPU reads / weak ordering, so
read-back-heavy paths may regress. Local pragmatic override, not intended
as-is for upstream (the clean fix is to tag these buffers USWC in the
guest radeonsi driver so the existing propagation below yields WC).

--- a/src/drm/amdgpu/amdgpu_renderer.c
+++ b/src/drm/amdgpu/amdgpu_renderer.c
@@ -415,10 +415,13 @@
       return -ENOENT;
    }
 
-   if (obj->enable_cache_wc)
-      blob->map_info = VIRGL_RENDERER_MAP_CACHE_WC;
-   else
-      blob->map_info = VIRGL_RENDERER_MAP_CACHE_CACHED;
+   /* Force write-combining for all host-visible blob mappings: write-back
+    * caching of host blobs causes severe CPU-write stalls over the virtio
+    * native context (radeonsi/RADV upload & staging buffers used by the
+    * compositor for texture uploads). Requires QEMU
+    * -accel kvm,honor-guest-pat=on. Trade-off: slower CPU reads.
+    */
+   blob->map_info = VIRGL_RENDERER_MAP_CACHE_WC;
 
    /* a memory can only be exported once; we don't want two resources to point
     * to the same storage.
